WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.371 --> 00:00:05.138
- Hello Believe Nation,
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.513
My one word is believe,

00:00:06.513 --> 00:00:08.247
and I believe that entrepreneurs are going

00:00:08.247 --> 00:00:11.431
to solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:11.431 --> 00:00:13.127
I started the Mentor
Me series with the goal

00:00:13.127 --> 00:00:16.022
to try to learn from people
who've done a lot more than us.

00:00:16.022 --> 00:00:17.822
People who have done amazing things,

00:00:17.822 --> 00:00:20.342
that by spending a little
bit more time with them,

00:00:20.342 --> 00:00:22.456
hopefully some of their
values, their belief systems,

00:00:22.456 --> 00:00:24.616
their way of thinking seeps into us,

00:00:24.616 --> 00:00:27.567
to help us become the
best version of ourselves.

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:28.876
So to help you on your journey today,

00:00:28.876 --> 00:00:30.579
we're going to learn
from Brendon Burchard,

00:00:30.579 --> 00:00:33.162
and some of his best advice on motivation.

00:00:33.162 --> 00:00:34.177
Mentor me Brendon.

00:00:34.177 --> 00:00:35.718
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:35.718 --> 00:00:38.126
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:38.126 --> 00:00:39.498
And as always guys as you're watching,

00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:41.921
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:41.921 --> 00:00:43.588
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:43.588 --> 00:00:44.998
and put quotes around it so other people

00:00:44.998 --> 00:00:46.731
can be inspired as well.

00:00:46.731 --> 00:00:48.047
And when you write it down,

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:51.507
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself too.

00:00:51.507 --> 00:00:52.583
Enjoy.

00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:56.250
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:01:05.206 --> 00:01:07.478
- Why is it sometimes you're
so motivated and driven,

00:01:07.478 --> 00:01:09.469
you're excited to go and do something.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.509
And other days you can't
tear yourself off the couch

00:01:11.509 --> 00:01:14.044
away from the fifth season of Netflix.

00:01:14.044 --> 00:01:15.512
What's the difference?

00:01:15.512 --> 00:01:17.492
Why is it some people are
so much more successful

00:01:17.492 --> 00:01:19.855
because they have that drive, that hunger,

00:01:19.855 --> 00:01:22.082
that ambition, that clarity?

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:26.627
And others struggle over and
over and over to get ahead?

00:01:26.627 --> 00:01:30.373
The whole thing comes down
to, as you know, motivation.

00:01:30.373 --> 00:01:31.206
But most people don't know

00:01:31.206 --> 00:01:32.465
where motivation really comes from.

00:01:32.465 --> 00:01:35.964
And we think hopefully one day,
we'll just have motivation.

00:01:35.964 --> 00:01:37.791
You know, we'll wake up and be motivated.

00:01:37.791 --> 00:01:41.651
But my favorite metaphor to
teach people is this one,

00:01:41.651 --> 00:01:45.818
the power plant doesn't have
energy, it generates energy.

00:01:47.771 --> 00:01:51.022
In the same way we don't have motivation,

00:01:51.022 --> 00:01:53.283
we generate motivation.

00:01:53.283 --> 00:01:55.353
And once you understand
the science of motivation,

00:01:55.353 --> 00:01:58.441
when you understand where
motivation actually comes from,

00:01:58.441 --> 00:02:01.141
now you know how to
cultivate it, and grow it.

00:02:01.141 --> 00:02:03.302
And that's what I spent the last 20 years

00:02:03.302 --> 00:02:06.561
of my life researching and studying.

00:02:06.561 --> 00:02:11.419
The first thing that sparks
motivation is ambition.

00:02:11.419 --> 00:02:14.152
Ambition is that desire
for something more.

00:02:14.152 --> 00:02:16.414
I know that's so simple,
but hold on a second.

00:02:16.414 --> 00:02:18.146
Because most people's ambition

00:02:18.146 --> 00:02:20.872
is set too low for themselves.

00:02:20.872 --> 00:02:23.260
They settled down on their ambition

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.800
because one time they were disappointed.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.868
One time, somebody made fun of them.

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:29.804
Maybe their spouse, their partner,

00:02:29.804 --> 00:02:30.902
their girlfriend, their boyfriend,

00:02:30.902 --> 00:02:32.847
somebody around them doesn't support them

00:02:32.847 --> 00:02:35.062
and cheer them on when they have ideas,

00:02:35.062 --> 00:02:37.774
and so now their ambitions and
the major areas of their life

00:02:37.774 --> 00:02:39.619
are actually pretty low.

00:02:39.619 --> 00:02:40.946
And if I could tell anybody anything

00:02:40.946 --> 00:02:45.043
to get more motivation,
first get more ambition.

00:02:45.043 --> 00:02:47.413
Dream again my friend.

00:02:47.413 --> 00:02:50.439
Be okay that your dreams and
your vision for yourself,

00:02:50.439 --> 00:02:53.004
for your emotional
reality, for your health,

00:02:53.004 --> 00:02:55.075
for your finances, for
how much money you have,

00:02:55.075 --> 00:02:57.571
for what you contribute to the world.

00:02:57.571 --> 00:02:59.067
You have to dream of that again.

00:02:59.067 --> 00:03:00.004
You have to lay awake in bed

00:03:00.004 --> 00:03:02.174
and think about what you desire and want.

00:03:02.174 --> 00:03:04.399
And not just on New Year's once a year,

00:03:04.399 --> 00:03:07.616
every single day think,
"What do I really desire?

00:03:07.616 --> 00:03:08.719
"What do I really want?"

00:03:08.719 --> 00:03:11.015
Your ambitions must stay in front of you

00:03:11.015 --> 00:03:14.519
to keep that flame of motivation going.

00:03:14.519 --> 00:03:15.852
Never lose hope.

00:03:16.777 --> 00:03:19.646
That you have a single breath
within your body right now

00:03:19.646 --> 00:03:22.706
and that you are alive
in this moment, is hope.

00:03:22.706 --> 00:03:24.093
That you can see all these people

00:03:24.093 --> 00:03:27.373
walking on the streets smiling, is hope.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.734
That all these entrepreneurs are posting

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:32.958
their art online every single
day now, there is hope there.

00:03:32.958 --> 00:03:35.365
That there is a single
person out in this world

00:03:35.365 --> 00:03:39.532
who's soul is still burning
alive with love, is hope.

00:03:40.756 --> 00:03:42.826
You know it's so easy during these days

00:03:42.826 --> 00:03:44.466
when sometimes there's darkness,

00:03:44.466 --> 00:03:46.288
when you see all this
negative media coverage,

00:03:46.288 --> 00:03:48.267
or maybe you have a series of bad days,

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:50.157
or a series of bad weeks,

00:03:50.157 --> 00:03:52.306
or your lucky break just isn't coming,

00:03:52.306 --> 00:03:54.027
or you've been fighting for that dream,

00:03:54.027 --> 00:03:56.141
you just don't sense any of that progress

00:03:56.141 --> 00:04:00.265
that you just so need to feel
still enlivened and engaged,

00:04:00.265 --> 00:04:01.898
and enthusiastic about something.

00:04:01.898 --> 00:04:04.827
Or, somebody breaks up with
you, or you lose your job,

00:04:04.827 --> 00:04:06.720
or something happens with your health.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.756
Look, that's part of life,

00:04:08.756 --> 00:04:12.319
is there's going to be so many
struggles and disappointments,

00:04:12.319 --> 00:04:15.659
challenges, setbacks, dark days,

00:04:15.659 --> 00:04:18.797
and part of sustaining and
making through all of that

00:04:18.797 --> 00:04:20.464
is maintaining hope.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:23.704
And that hope isn't something
that just, you know,

00:04:23.704 --> 00:04:25.618
some airy fairy concept.

00:04:25.618 --> 00:04:30.257
It is a psychological need to
believe that we can endure.

00:04:30.257 --> 00:04:32.417
A psychological need to believe
that we can not only endure,

00:04:32.417 --> 00:04:34.342
but we can succeed and we can thrive,

00:04:34.342 --> 00:04:37.053
and we can have our way in the world

00:04:37.053 --> 00:04:38.751
so that we can accomplish our dreams,

00:04:38.751 --> 00:04:39.921
so that we can make influence,

00:04:39.921 --> 00:04:41.879
so we can make our own difference.

00:04:41.879 --> 00:04:46.046
To have hope we have to
stay persistent. Persistent.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:50.012
You know, to keep at it
no matter what, you know.

00:04:50.012 --> 00:04:53.106
If we've got our perspective
in mind, we've got our plan,

00:04:53.106 --> 00:04:54.817
we've got to be persistent.

00:04:54.817 --> 00:04:56.616
To keep working towards it.

00:04:56.616 --> 00:04:58.720
You know, there were so many times

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:00.839
that I almost stopped doing these videos.

00:05:00.839 --> 00:05:02.426
There are so many times that I thought,

00:05:02.426 --> 00:05:04.715
"Well, I'm not going
to write another book."

00:05:04.715 --> 00:05:05.548
There are so many times I thought,

00:05:05.548 --> 00:05:07.120
"No one cares about my blog posts.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.392
"No one cares about my Facebook posts.

00:05:09.392 --> 00:05:10.764
"No one cares about my YouTube show.

00:05:10.764 --> 00:05:13.158
"No one cares about me. Oh, woe is me."

00:05:13.158 --> 00:05:14.890
Look, we can all sit on the couch,

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:16.841
eat a bunch of potato chips,
watch stupid television,

00:05:16.841 --> 00:05:18.619
and feel sorry for ourselves.

00:05:18.619 --> 00:05:21.071
That does not contribute to our aliveness,

00:05:21.071 --> 00:05:22.793
it does not contribute to our connection

00:05:22.793 --> 00:05:24.370
with those we love and care for,

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:27.684
and it does not contribute
to the things that we create,

00:05:27.684 --> 00:05:29.765
and ultimately give to the world.

00:05:29.765 --> 00:05:32.836
So we've got to say, "You
know what, this is not what,

00:05:32.836 --> 00:05:34.490
"when are we going to persist at sitting

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:36.627
"and eating potato chips and watching TV?"

00:05:36.627 --> 00:05:38.173
That's not going to be good.

00:05:38.173 --> 00:05:41.595
What we have to do, is
persist towards our dreams.

00:05:41.595 --> 00:05:44.953
What are the three things
you can accomplish this day,

00:05:44.953 --> 00:05:46.904
this very day? And tomorrow?

00:05:46.904 --> 00:05:48.660
And start moving towards your dreams?

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.034
Everyday wake up with the intention,

00:05:50.034 --> 00:05:52.886
"I'm going to do at least three
things to move myself forward

00:05:52.886 --> 00:05:54.036
"to something that matters."

00:05:54.036 --> 00:05:55.521
At least three things.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:56.905
Everybody can do that.

00:05:56.905 --> 00:05:58.830
Just pick, "What are the
three things I'm going to do

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.523
"to move my life forward this day?

00:06:01.523 --> 00:06:04.459
"Who do I need to reach out
to to be able to move forward?

00:06:04.459 --> 00:06:07.845
"What can I read or study
online to move forward?

00:06:07.845 --> 00:06:08.745
"What can I do?"

00:06:08.745 --> 00:06:11.660
Just one simple request,
one simple movement,

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.412
one simple step to move forward,

00:06:13.412 --> 00:06:16.709
and persist at that, over
and over and over again.

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.551
And that's how things change.

00:06:18.551 --> 00:06:21.628
What is it that's going to
actually change somebody's life?

00:06:21.628 --> 00:06:24.452
It's not removing their limiting beliefs.

00:06:24.452 --> 00:06:27.010
And I know that sounds
silly, but it's like,

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:30.958
if you just put less pressure
on the brake in your car,

00:06:30.958 --> 00:06:32.983
it doesn't mean you're
going to speed up, right?

00:06:32.983 --> 00:06:34.580
Your foot's still on the brake.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.460
If you're always focusing on these things

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:38.834
that are limiting you, you're
always going to be limited

00:06:38.834 --> 00:06:41.220
just because your relative
weight of importance

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:42.696
and duration of your
focus and your attention

00:06:42.696 --> 00:06:45.047
is on these limiting things.

00:06:45.047 --> 00:06:46.858
And it's a time in our culture,

00:06:46.858 --> 00:06:48.855
just like in our psychology,

00:06:48.855 --> 00:06:50.332
in our study of psychology,

00:06:50.332 --> 00:06:53.584
we've got to move from mental
illness to mental health.

00:06:53.584 --> 00:06:56.564
We've got to get you to move
from your limiting beliefs,

00:06:56.564 --> 00:07:00.918
into something bigger and
greater and grand about yourself.

00:07:00.918 --> 00:07:03.212
We've got to stop you
focusing on all the reasons

00:07:03.212 --> 00:07:04.484
that you're a mouse in life,

00:07:04.484 --> 00:07:06.859
and start focusing on why you're a lion.

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:08.501
Why you have something within you

00:07:08.501 --> 00:07:10.440
that's more bold and powerful and profound

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:12.598
than you've ever even knew.

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:14.017
So what we have to do is change

00:07:14.017 --> 00:07:17.935
what I call your dominant
frame of attention and focus.

00:07:17.935 --> 00:07:19.741
Most people's dominant frame,

00:07:19.741 --> 00:07:21.736
they're giving that relative
weight of importance

00:07:21.736 --> 00:07:23.231
to those things that limit them.

00:07:23.231 --> 00:07:25.278
And I say, "You know what, this year,

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:27.911
"this next year has to be the year for you

00:07:27.911 --> 00:07:29.768
"that you're limitless."

00:07:29.768 --> 00:07:32.815
That you're going to go, "Okay, enough."

00:07:32.815 --> 00:07:34.998
I mean how far have you
gotten in your life now

00:07:34.998 --> 00:07:37.045
where you're just
constantly beating yourself

00:07:37.045 --> 00:07:39.309
and berating yourself and
worrying about your limits?

00:07:39.309 --> 00:07:40.738
And worrying about all these things,

00:07:40.738 --> 00:07:43.641
of all the reasons that
you have to be worried,

00:07:43.641 --> 00:07:47.150
to be weak, to be less than you are.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.613
You know it's like when
Mary Ann Williamson

00:07:48.613 --> 00:07:50.521
said so long ago, "You
are not serving the world

00:07:50.521 --> 00:07:51.963
"by playing small."

00:07:51.963 --> 00:07:54.113
And you're not serving the
world by constantly focusing

00:07:54.113 --> 00:07:56.397
on your limiting beliefs
and trying to remove them.

00:07:56.397 --> 00:08:00.103
Look, you will always have insecurity.

00:08:00.103 --> 00:08:01.292
I know that's really motivating,

00:08:01.292 --> 00:08:02.664
but you're always going to have it.

00:08:02.664 --> 00:08:04.533
I work with some of the top professionals

00:08:04.533 --> 00:08:05.799
in every given field.

00:08:05.799 --> 00:08:07.351
Some of the best athletes in the world,

00:08:07.351 --> 00:08:09.196
some of the best well-known celebrities

00:08:09.196 --> 00:08:11.586
and many of the people who
are the best performers

00:08:11.586 --> 00:08:13.015
in any given industry.

00:08:13.015 --> 00:08:14.244
And I can tell you,

00:08:14.244 --> 00:08:17.432
they still have their
doubts and their fears.

00:08:17.432 --> 00:08:19.175
They still have times when they wake up

00:08:19.175 --> 00:08:20.086
and they're just like,

00:08:20.086 --> 00:08:21.336
"I don't know what to do with myself."

00:08:21.336 --> 00:08:22.978
That doesn't ever go away,

00:08:22.978 --> 00:08:25.285
and that's great because it's
part of the human condition

00:08:25.285 --> 00:08:28.120
that also makes us
humble, it makes us real,

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:30.426
it makes us check ourselves.

00:08:30.426 --> 00:08:32.192
And I'm not saying that, you know,

00:08:32.192 --> 00:08:35.252
we all have to go around being
happy optimists all the time.

00:08:35.252 --> 00:08:37.344
But I will share with
you, if you didn't know,

00:08:37.344 --> 00:08:39.662
optimists are much more
capable of changing the world

00:08:39.662 --> 00:08:40.936
than pessimists are.

00:08:40.936 --> 00:08:43.419
It's not a guess, it's proven by science.

00:08:43.419 --> 00:08:44.600
And what do we mean by that?

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.895
Optimism is one of the most studied thing,

00:08:46.895 --> 00:08:49.505
in the psychology literature, period.

00:08:49.505 --> 00:08:50.596
It's one of the most studied traits.

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:55.208
Optimists are more likely to
face a problem than pessimists.

00:08:55.208 --> 00:08:57.753
'Cause pessimists go,
"Oh, I can't change it,

00:08:57.753 --> 00:08:59.261
"I can't do anything about it,

00:08:59.261 --> 00:09:00.971
"it's going to be that way forever,

00:09:00.971 --> 00:09:03.716
"it's a pervasive problem and
I don't have a control of it."

00:09:03.716 --> 00:09:05.955
An optimist says, "Well, I
can probably handle that.

00:09:05.955 --> 00:09:07.961
"We can change that too."

00:09:07.961 --> 00:09:10.663
In other words, pessimists
tend to avoid problems

00:09:10.663 --> 00:09:11.810
that need to be changed,

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:13.748
and optimists tend to confront them

00:09:13.748 --> 00:09:15.910
and move forward, and
do something about it.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:18.882
That's pretty profound,
and it's pretty proven now.

00:09:18.882 --> 00:09:20.895
So yeah, I'm saying, you know,

00:09:20.895 --> 00:09:23.483
while not all of us can go
around being happy-go-lucky,

00:09:23.483 --> 00:09:25.226
and avoiding all of our limits,

00:09:25.226 --> 00:09:26.869
I'm also saying, you know what,

00:09:26.869 --> 00:09:28.916
maybe it is time that
we focus on those things

00:09:28.916 --> 00:09:30.105
that we can change.

00:09:30.105 --> 00:09:32.490
Focus on something that's
bigger than ourselves,

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:34.762
and our own little
insecurities and worries.

00:09:34.762 --> 00:09:37.037
And I think that's the
challenge right now,

00:09:37.037 --> 00:09:38.120
with so many people saying,

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.726
"Limiting beliefs, limiting beliefs."

00:09:39.726 --> 00:09:41.131
Look, they're there.

00:09:41.131 --> 00:09:42.413
You're going to have them.

00:09:42.413 --> 00:09:45.295
The question is, are they
going to win the day?

00:09:45.295 --> 00:09:49.156
Your peers have a lot to do
with the setting long-term,

00:09:49.156 --> 00:09:52.532
of your health, of your
drive, of your success,

00:09:52.532 --> 00:09:54.714
of your social economic status.

00:09:54.714 --> 00:09:56.204
The people that you hang out with

00:09:56.204 --> 00:09:58.370
impact your life tremendously.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:00.723
So your environment, do
you have the right people?

00:10:00.723 --> 00:10:02.239
If you don't have great people around you,

00:10:02.239 --> 00:10:03.353
I always tell people,

00:10:03.353 --> 00:10:06.292
go to a seminar, get in
personal development,

00:10:06.292 --> 00:10:09.932
go volunteer, go do things
with your church group.

00:10:09.932 --> 00:10:13.276
But just get out there with
people who are like-minded,

00:10:13.276 --> 00:10:15.268
who want to grow, and want to give.

00:10:15.268 --> 00:10:17.190
'Cause if you're around people
who want to grow and give

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:20.365
all day long, you become stronger,

00:10:20.365 --> 00:10:22.255
and you contribute more too.

00:10:22.255 --> 00:10:26.061
And suddenly, you find more
motivation and fulfillment.

00:10:26.061 --> 00:10:27.505
Here's a very simple thing you can do

00:10:27.505 --> 00:10:29.095
to re-program your mind.

00:10:29.095 --> 00:10:32.504
Create a sheet of two simple
things, very simple things.

00:10:32.504 --> 00:10:35.339
I want you to write five questions down,

00:10:35.339 --> 00:10:39.074
that you're going to ask yourself
three or four times a day.

00:10:39.074 --> 00:10:41.494
Five questions that are positive,
for yourself in general.

00:10:41.494 --> 00:10:43.225
Everyday you're going to
wake up in the morning,

00:10:43.225 --> 00:10:44.822
you're going to read these
questions to yourself,

00:10:44.822 --> 00:10:45.711
you're going to answer 'em.

00:10:45.711 --> 00:10:47.072
You're going to read 'em,
you're going to answer 'em.

00:10:47.072 --> 00:10:47.905
Every morning.

00:10:47.905 --> 00:10:50.199
Then at lunch, read the
questions, answer 'em.

00:10:50.199 --> 00:10:52.639
At night, read the questions, answer 'em.

00:10:52.639 --> 00:10:53.628
These can be questions like,

00:10:53.628 --> 00:10:56.789
what can I feel incredibly
grateful for right now?

00:10:56.789 --> 00:10:59.950
How could I surprise or flirt
with somebody right now?

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:02.255
How could I have fun right now?

00:11:02.255 --> 00:11:03.774
Positive things like that, right?

00:11:03.774 --> 00:11:07.320
How could I demonstrate love
or excellence right now?

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:08.591
Ask these questions in the morning,

00:11:08.591 --> 00:11:10.963
ask in the afternoon, ask 'em at night.

00:11:10.963 --> 00:11:13.482
By asking these positive
questions over and over,

00:11:13.482 --> 00:11:15.040
I mean you just do this for 30 days,

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:17.867
you're going to recognize
a total shift in your life.

00:11:17.867 --> 00:11:19.184
Just simple questions.

00:11:19.184 --> 00:11:21.636
But you're giving them weight,

00:11:21.636 --> 00:11:24.235
by focusing on 'em three
times during the day.

00:11:24.235 --> 00:11:26.023
You're having duration by focusing on it

00:11:26.023 --> 00:11:27.958
three times during the day over 30 days.

00:11:27.958 --> 00:11:29.972
Your mind starts to re-shift it's gears,

00:11:29.972 --> 00:11:33.369
to give automatic ease to
answering those questions

00:11:33.369 --> 00:11:35.588
and living in that mindset,

00:11:35.588 --> 00:11:38.597
versus an undirected, unconscious mindset.

00:11:38.597 --> 00:11:40.970
Second thing on that sheet,
or those things you can do,

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.454
five questions first,

00:11:42.454 --> 00:11:43.579
second thing I want you to do,

00:11:43.579 --> 00:11:46.539
is come up with three words
that describe your ideal self.

00:11:46.539 --> 00:11:48.294
Just, three words you know?

00:11:48.294 --> 00:11:52.939
Mine are for example,
present, excited and bold.

00:11:52.939 --> 00:11:54.323
So I'm going to focus on those questions

00:11:54.323 --> 00:11:55.538
three times a day as well.

00:11:55.538 --> 00:11:57.451
What I do is I put 'em on my iPhone,

00:11:57.451 --> 00:11:58.926
and they come up as an alarm,

00:11:58.926 --> 00:11:59.954
three different times during the day.

00:11:59.954 --> 00:12:02.339
Just my phone buzzes, and
those words are there.

00:12:02.339 --> 00:12:05.032
I'm like, "Oh right, I'm that guy."

00:12:05.032 --> 00:12:07.553
I got to focus on being
that guy versus whatever,

00:12:07.553 --> 00:12:08.612
I might be in a bad mood.

00:12:08.612 --> 00:12:09.732
I'm like aah!

00:12:09.732 --> 00:12:10.822
You know, completely detached,

00:12:10.822 --> 00:12:14.511
and I look, I'm like, "Dude,
no I'm an excited person.

00:12:14.511 --> 00:12:16.316
"Break that thought, get back into this.

00:12:16.316 --> 00:12:18.578
"Got it, this is who I am."

00:12:18.578 --> 00:12:20.827
And now that might sound so simpy, simple.

00:12:20.827 --> 00:12:22.180
Simpy? Simpy.

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:24.441
That sounds so simple, but guess what?

00:12:24.441 --> 00:12:26.332
People won't do the discipline.

00:12:26.332 --> 00:12:28.412
They are so frustrated
with their mind because

00:12:28.412 --> 00:12:30.776
they haven't done the
conscience discipline

00:12:30.776 --> 00:12:32.175
to re-program it.

00:12:32.175 --> 00:12:36.342
The first idea is to emotionally
engage with that dream,

00:12:38.289 --> 00:12:40.456
each morning of your life.

00:12:41.585 --> 00:12:43.678
See, a lot of people
don't actually struggle

00:12:43.678 --> 00:12:47.629
with the discipline part, in
terms of the doing the thing.

00:12:47.629 --> 00:12:51.263
It's that, they are not getting
revved up to do the thing.

00:12:51.263 --> 00:12:53.783
In other words we got a
problem with motivation,

00:12:53.783 --> 00:12:55.740
not necessarily just discipline.

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.024
We have a problem with,
that once in awhile,

00:12:58.024 --> 00:13:00.487
you hit it, you do it, you do the work.

00:13:00.487 --> 00:13:01.992
But a lot of times you fall off,

00:13:01.992 --> 00:13:04.264
because you're not
emotionally engaged in it.

00:13:04.264 --> 00:13:06.210
It's like, if you want
a lot of discipline,

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:09.653
you need a high level
of emotional connection

00:13:09.653 --> 00:13:12.600
and focus on that thing that
you want to work towards.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:13.871
So every morning what I want you to do,

00:13:13.871 --> 00:13:16.333
is just start a new
visualization practice.

00:13:16.333 --> 00:13:18.763
When you wake up in the
morning, close your eyes,

00:13:18.763 --> 00:13:21.429
think about the dream, the aspiration,

00:13:21.429 --> 00:13:24.365
the thing that you're
really after in life,

00:13:24.365 --> 00:13:25.929
and just visualize it.

00:13:25.929 --> 00:13:28.168
And really get yourself
emotionally attached,

00:13:28.168 --> 00:13:29.765
emotionally engaged with it.

00:13:29.765 --> 00:13:31.542
Think about how great it will feel,

00:13:31.542 --> 00:13:34.231
for you to have that
thing, or be that thing,

00:13:34.231 --> 00:13:37.673
or contribute that thing,
to make that difference.

00:13:37.673 --> 00:13:39.462
Just think about, allow it to well up

00:13:39.462 --> 00:13:42.000
in your heart a little
bit, get excited about it.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.890
Remember the dream.

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:45.341
That's why we get away from discipline,

00:13:45.341 --> 00:13:47.501
because we're so busy with
the chaos of the world,

00:13:47.501 --> 00:13:51.184
that we emotionally are no
longer attached in a way

00:13:51.184 --> 00:13:53.761
that our brain says,
"Hey man, focus on this.

00:13:53.761 --> 00:13:56.647
"It's important to remember."

00:13:56.647 --> 00:13:59.392
So if your heart is disengaged,

00:13:59.392 --> 00:14:02.249
it's difficult to stay disciplined.

00:14:02.249 --> 00:14:05.332
So every morning make it a practice

00:14:05.332 --> 00:14:08.414
to actually just imagine the payoff,

00:14:08.414 --> 00:14:11.013
the benefit, the contribution, the art,

00:14:11.013 --> 00:14:14.770
the thing that you do, and
are doing, and do contribute.

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:16.397
If you can do that more often,

00:14:16.397 --> 00:14:19.888
you'll be more fired up, and
you'll stay back on track.

00:14:19.888 --> 00:14:23.116
You have to actually show up every day,

00:14:23.116 --> 00:14:27.154
and inch yourself forward
toward these dreams.

00:14:27.154 --> 00:14:28.729
And not only show up every day,

00:14:28.729 --> 00:14:30.491
and once in awhile inch yourself.

00:14:30.491 --> 00:14:34.270
I mean every day, you have
to actually take an action

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:35.430
that moves you forward,

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.725
not just research, not just thinking.

00:14:37.725 --> 00:14:40.191
Look, the power of intention is great,

00:14:40.191 --> 00:14:42.655
but without any initiative it's dead.

00:14:42.655 --> 00:14:44.207
Right? A dream is great,

00:14:44.207 --> 00:14:47.030
but without any movement it's dead.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:50.114
You have to be moving towards every day.

00:14:50.114 --> 00:14:51.688
You can send an email every day,

00:14:51.688 --> 00:14:53.285
you can make a call every day,

00:14:53.285 --> 00:14:54.703
you can write something every day,

00:14:54.703 --> 00:14:55.851
you can create something every day,

00:14:55.851 --> 00:14:56.964
you can contribute something every day.

00:14:56.964 --> 00:14:59.236
But it has to be daily,

00:14:59.236 --> 00:15:02.691
otherwise it will never become actualized.

00:15:02.691 --> 00:15:04.171
The highest performers in
the world didn't get there

00:15:04.171 --> 00:15:05.588
'cause they were lucky,

00:15:05.588 --> 00:15:07.984
they worked at it longer
than everyone else.

00:15:07.984 --> 00:15:09.582
They had a better work ethic.

00:15:09.582 --> 00:15:12.079
And it's not that they
necessarily always worked harder,

00:15:12.079 --> 00:15:15.184
they worked smarter because
they were doing the research,

00:15:15.184 --> 00:15:17.288
they were taking the time to visualize

00:15:17.288 --> 00:15:19.808
how they would be distinct, different,

00:15:19.808 --> 00:15:21.439
how they would survive the tough times.

00:15:21.439 --> 00:15:23.464
They really kept at it.

00:15:23.464 --> 00:15:26.547
Keep every single day momentum going,

00:15:27.851 --> 00:15:29.922
and if you don't do
that, there's no chance.

00:15:29.922 --> 00:15:31.856
In the psychology literature,

00:15:31.856 --> 00:15:34.905
expectancy means it's a belief

00:15:34.905 --> 00:15:37.561
that not only is it possible for you,

00:15:37.561 --> 00:15:39.151
but that you can do it.

00:15:39.151 --> 00:15:42.167
That you have the personal
control, the self-reliance,

00:15:42.167 --> 00:15:44.586
the autonomy, the thing that says,

00:15:44.586 --> 00:15:47.859
"You know what, I believe in
my ability to figure this out,

00:15:47.859 --> 00:15:51.254
"and I know I can move the
needle of progress forward

00:15:51.254 --> 00:15:52.221
"in going this."

00:15:52.221 --> 00:15:55.191
In other words, you expect
your dreams to happen,

00:15:55.191 --> 00:15:57.430
and you expect that you have the strength

00:15:57.430 --> 00:15:59.950
and the confidence to make it happen.

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:04.090
The challenge is, I know so
many people in the world,

00:16:04.090 --> 00:16:06.025
who sometimes they have the dream

00:16:06.025 --> 00:16:07.398
but the ambition goes away

00:16:07.398 --> 00:16:08.612
'cause of other people around them.

00:16:08.612 --> 00:16:11.494
Sometimes they have the
ambition and the dream,

00:16:11.494 --> 00:16:12.669
but they don't really believe

00:16:12.669 --> 00:16:15.645
in themselves deep down inside.

